      "writtenOn": "2021-11-17T18:56:25Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "For what it’s worth, for v8.dev we decided to use semantic newlines only in Markdown source files, i.e. no hard-wrapping at all, only adding a newline when the actual content contains one. (The markdown-it config that goes with that is `breaks: true`.) Perhaps something worth considering for this site as well?",
      "parentUuid": "03ee61fd_52044289",
      "revId": "682f4cfe5e474c62c791170ce95c761e655e357f",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
